WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.900
LG just opened free API access to its 750 billion K, ExaOwn 2.5 model for agentic workloads. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 229. Telecom operators are putting agents on live networks, Simon Willison has a Github Collapse trick for AI pull requests, then things to try. LG AI research, according to MK, continued training from the August K, ExaOwn 2.0 release, into a mixture of expert system, an architecture that routes each token

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.380
through only a subset of specialist networks with strong Korean language support.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:40.440
The model handles long contacts plus complex tool calls, and internal benchmarks show gains

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:46.160
over the prior version on software development, web information retrieval, software as a service,

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:49.600
or SAS, automation, and agent problem solving tasks.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:54.800
Developers and startups can obtain an API key immediately through the Exa-owned platform

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.360
for service building and research.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:01.140
The release is a technology validation step toward a frontier level system planned

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:07.640
for January. Telecom operators, PYM and TS reports, are assigning AI agents, expanded

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:13.260
roles in network operations, customer service, and predictive maintenance, a shift that reflects

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:19.297
growing trust and agent reliability for high stakes infrastructure tasks. Go emotions tests

00:01:19.297 --> 00:01:25.657
of seven large language models, or LLMs, in an archive NLP paper, show consistent over

00:01:25.657 --> 00:01:31.237
compression of 27 fine-grained emotion categories into broader positive negative splits in their

00:01:31.237 --> 00:01:35.977
hidden representations. Linear probes still recover that fine-grained information,

00:01:36.197 --> 00:01:41.988
even though the unsupervised geometry favors coarser groupings. Wikipedia editors and students

00:01:41.988 --> 00:01:47.548
identify AI texts using diverse evidence types that prove contradictory and context dependent

00:01:47.548 --> 00:01:53.668
rather than fixed textual markers. And pragmatic infallicity, the sense that the wording is often

00:01:53.668 --> 00:01:57.928
in context, often drives those judgments rather than any specific feature.

00:01:58.428 --> 00:02:03.088
RL attack trains a reinforcement learning attacker against target models and achieves

00:02:03.088 --> 00:02:08.528
lower post-attack accuracy and better query efficiency than baselines on natural language

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:13.428
inference and generative question answering, learning tailored transformations directly from

00:02:13.428 --> 00:02:15.208
the target without external knowledge.

00:02:15.748 --> 00:02:21.728
Biomedical fine-tune models, 25 of them audited against their base checkpoints, saw appropriate

00:02:21.728 --> 00:02:28.748
abstention rates on Metabstain drop from a median of 8.3% to 4.2% after fine-tuning, and

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:34.288
the change was heterogeneous across model pairs. Simon Willison, in a post on X, reports

00:02:34.288 --> 00:02:38.928
selectively copying sentences generated by agents into his own writing when they match

00:02:38.928 --> 00:02:44.028
his intended meaning exactly, treating agents as collaborative drafting tools rather than

00:02:44.028 --> 00:02:50.248
full replacements. Github Markdown, his blog notes, supports HTML details and summary tags,

00:02:50.248 --> 00:02:55.788
So, he now collapses lengthy AI-generated pull request descriptions behind them, keeping

00:02:55.788 --> 00:02:58.268
the content available while cutting reader fatigue.

00:02:59.329 --> 00:03:04.989
Agent skills procedural descriptions and archive NLP paper shows can yield authorization

00:03:04.989 --> 00:03:08.209
requirements used to train sub-agent permission policies.

00:03:08.629 --> 00:03:15.089
On Claw Arena team that raised tool permission precision by 13.4 points and workspace permission

00:03:15.089 --> 00:03:23.819
precision by 24.1 points for QN 3.535 BA3B. Mars trains multilingual search agents that

00:03:23.819 --> 00:03:28.319
interact directly with raw corpora via shell commands instead of relying on learned

00:03:28.319 --> 00:03:34.079
retrievers and corpus native entity grounding plus redundancy aware rewards improve trajectory

00:03:34.079 --> 00:03:39.959
quality and cross-lingual generalization. Twitter preview cards willis and found in a post

00:03:39.959 --> 00:03:45.719
on X, strip, or break HTML tags placed in post titles, which affects anyone embedding

00:03:45.719 --> 00:03:51.319
formatted text in social sharing metadata. Men seeking mental health support, stat reports,

00:03:51.639 --> 00:03:56.519
are being studied as a case for whether AI chatbots can lower barriers even though those systems

00:03:56.519 --> 00:04:02.399
are not licensed therapists, with the piece focusing on conversational patterns that encourage disclosure.

00:04:03.099 --> 00:04:07.119
Survey history is structured as background, decision procedure, and evaluation,

00:04:07.119 --> 00:04:21.319
An archive NLP paper found improved held out answer prediction accuracy over raw transcripts by 1.27 points on GPT-5.4 nano and 1.19 points on GPT-5.4 mini

00:04:21.319 --> 00:04:24.939
and adding the evaluation component drove most of the gain.

00:04:25.499 --> 00:04:35.479
GPT-2 recursively self-trained on its own outputs produces distinct crossing points where different Renny entropy measures shift from loss to gain as sampling temperature rises

00:04:35.479 --> 00:04:39.699
And that ordering holds across multiple measurement protocols and languages.

00:04:40.339 --> 00:04:45.619
In papers on archive today, due calculus remains sound, but loses completeness when identifying

00:04:45.619 --> 00:04:50.339
causal effects from arbitrary mixtures of observational and interventional distributions.

00:04:50.979 --> 00:04:56.119
An entailment-based illusion controller removes surplus tokens while preserving content better

00:04:56.119 --> 00:05:02.079
than simple truncation on three model families, though 59% of sample delusions still harmed

00:05:02.079 --> 00:05:02.899
answer quality.

00:05:02.899 --> 00:05:08.819
GPT-2 models trained on tiny stories produced higher-brain alignment scores than code-trained

00:05:08.819 --> 00:05:15.679
counterparts on Pereira 243 and Tuck-Ute 2024, with the advantage tied to natural language

00:05:15.679 --> 00:05:17.759
training rather than abstract structure.

00:05:18.339 --> 00:05:23.619
FPRT profiles student failure modes and selects teacher trajectories reachable by the student,

00:05:24.099 --> 00:05:28.739
achieving state-of-the-art results across five reasoning benchmarks on two student backbones.

00:05:28.739 --> 00:05:33.259
Muslims. Human Raiders found no consistent advantage for reasoning-enhanced models on

00:05:33.259 --> 00:05:39.179
short-story psychological depth, while an LLM as a judge showed strong pro-reasoning bias.

00:05:39.859 --> 00:05:44.199
Automatic metrics failed to detect script spillage and English collapse in romanized

00:05:44.199 --> 00:05:49.559
Hindi, Telugu, and Kannada generation, while native speakers rated outputs differently across

00:05:49.559 --> 00:05:55.159
four frontier models. Alien Bench scores model descriptions of alien creatures by counting

00:05:55.159 --> 00:06:00.119
departures from Earth-animal features, with open-weight models averaging higher novelty

00:06:00.119 --> 00:06:01.399
than proprietary ones.

00:06:01.899 --> 00:06:08.139
Plane Transformer classifiers on 22.1 million tokens matched or beat bidirectional LSTM

00:06:08.139 --> 00:06:14.099
CRF variants in 7 of 8 matched comparisons, showing recurrent and structured heads add little

00:06:14.099 --> 00:06:15.479
under fixed training budgets.

00:06:16.349 --> 00:06:21.299
Calibrated concept profiles turn direct neuron reading into a repeatable measurement by sampling

00:06:21.299 --> 00:06:26.739
a declared stimulus distribution and reporting activation in units of the Neuron's own spread.

00:06:27.219 --> 00:06:32.679
OpenCoder 1.5b kept changing which Neuron's carry any given Python construct through

00:06:32.679 --> 00:06:37.019
the final checkpoint even after loss on grammar fixed positions had plateaued.

00:06:37.439 --> 00:06:42.539
Post-trained models supplied more valid but less varied references than base models for the first

00:06:42.539 --> 00:06:48.039
judge-free Kamehra open-ended generation benchmark. Clear generates knowledge matched question

00:06:48.039 --> 00:06:53.619
pairs that vary application demand while holding required facts constant, exposing application

00:06:53.619 --> 00:06:55.639
failures even when knowledge is supplied.

00:06:56.179 --> 00:07:02.479
Duet applies prefix key value sparsity and early query sparsity to achieve 1.34 times to

00:07:02.479 --> 00:07:12.899
2.83 times speed ups on LLA-DA-2.1 mini and 2.41 times to 4.72 times on SDR-8B-Chat-B32

00:07:12.899 --> 00:07:20.579
at 32,000 contexts. European hospitals, seven of them created 699 artificial cardiology reports

00:07:20.579 --> 00:07:26.519
across seven languages, with a 94 patient parallel subset providing sentence-align translations

00:07:26.519 --> 00:07:32.619
from model adaptation. A split latent method isolates acoustic word embeddings from style embeddings,

00:07:33.079 --> 00:07:38.979
revealing that vocal tract filter features dominate lexical clustering while F0 dynamics dominate

00:07:38.979 --> 00:07:45.099
speaker clustering. Sin2DRE, a lightweight teacher student setup with cross-supervision and unified

00:07:45.099 --> 00:07:50.899
end-to-end training, outperformed prior semi-supervised document-level relation extraction methods on

00:07:50.899 --> 00:07:56.559
multiple benchmarks. The two-stage Apex retriever first selects candidate-intense via prototypes,

00:07:57.119 --> 00:08:04.049
then retrieves exemplars inside that intense space, lifting exact match accuracy by 4.34 points on

00:08:04.049 --> 00:08:09.809
when 3-4-B. Open-weight LLMs without fine-tuning already surpassed three fine-tuned

00:08:09.809 --> 00:08:15.149
BERT baselines on Danish hate speech detection, with further lightweight fine-tuning widening

00:08:15.149 --> 00:08:20.009
the gap. Truncating speaker embeddings below the full voice activity segment degraded

00:08:20.009 --> 00:08:24.789
every tested and better, while denoising before embedding raised equal error rates across

00:08:24.789 --> 00:08:30.849
architectures. QGPM, a training-free method, reshapes rotary positions using query relevance

00:08:30.849 --> 00:08:36.329
from the model's own attention heads and improved retrieval on no-lima and ruler across multiple

00:08:36.329 --> 00:08:42.289
context lengths. Ru act assigns unreachable rubrics the teacher role and saturated rubrics the

00:08:42.289 --> 00:08:48.069
critic role, raising recovery rates and reward quality alignment on medical and scientific benchmarks.

00:08:48.769 --> 00:08:53.969
Lambda Mix trains one low-rank adapter per objective and mixes them at inference according to a

00:08:53.969 --> 00:08:58.929
preference vector, achieving higher hypervolume than specialist or merging baselines on

00:08:58.929 --> 00:09:01.769
helpfulness, harmlessness, and math instruction tasks.

00:09:02.429 --> 00:09:08.389
Passage budget increases on 1,100 beam questions raised mean scores, but gains diminished

00:09:08.389 --> 00:09:12.449
at higher budgets while abstention scores sometimes rose as context shrank.

00:09:13.089 --> 00:09:18.069
Linguistic range and politeness strategy altered neither trust, votes, nor night actions in

00:09:18.069 --> 00:09:21.389
30 lurk, werewolf games after multiple comparison correction.

00:09:22.129 --> 00:09:27.529
Rose restricts edits to orthogonal compliments of prior subspaces while using risk masks to

00:09:27.529 --> 00:09:32.749
and protect stability critical parameters, maintaining performance across 1,000 sequential

00:09:32.749 --> 00:09:33.769
multimodal edits.

00:09:34.349 --> 00:09:38.949
Prompt-supplied contextual meanings overroad prior lexical knowledge, more often for

00:09:38.949 --> 00:09:44.069
low frequency words and supportive sentence contexts, with larger models showing stronger

00:09:44.069 --> 00:09:45.149
contextual reliance.

00:09:45.749 --> 00:09:52.869
Atomic fact, compaction outperformed raw transcript retrieval on low-como by 6.8 points at 34% fewer

00:09:52.869 --> 00:09:56.489
tokens when answers depended on values rather than phrasing.

00:09:57.289 --> 00:10:02.849
CodeQuant2, a clustering-based lookup table quantizer with rotation, scaling, and layer-adaptive

00:10:02.849 --> 00:10:09.029
codebooks, delivered accuracy gains on reasoning benchmarks plus up to 2.85 times speed up over

00:10:09.029 --> 00:10:15.129
BF-16. A hybrid knowledge graph plus dense vector pipeline with semantic chunking outperformed

00:10:15.129 --> 00:10:21.329
standalone vector and graph baselines on the multi-hop rag dataset. Participation ratio slopes

00:10:21.329 --> 00:10:26.829
against subsample size separate into a sampling floor and an axis-aligned shift, and only

00:10:26.829 --> 00:10:30.909
the latter tracks known symmetries in mouse v1 and language model layers.

00:10:31.609 --> 00:10:36.269
Bias teachers transferred animal and facial preferences to students through numbers generated

00:10:36.269 --> 00:10:41.969
on an unrelated geometric task, with transfer strength increasing alongside training data volume.

00:10:42.469 --> 00:10:48.029
Standard int4 and principal component analysis compression lost more sparse autoencoder features

00:10:48.029 --> 00:10:54.129
than a random receipt on GPT-2 and Pithia caches, while per channel standardization recovered

00:10:54.129 --> 00:10:59.369
performance at the same file size. The first Turkish video fact checking data set was paired

00:10:59.369 --> 00:11:06.909
with a 3 million fact TR agent pipeline, and a Laura fine-tuned Quinn 2.57B, both evaluated

00:11:06.909 --> 00:11:13.229
on accuracy and macro F-1. Chainflow, a flow matching drafter conditioned on target hidden states,

00:11:13.229 --> 00:11:22.389
achieve 39% and 11% higher speedups than Eagle 3 and D Flash respectively on QN 3.5 models inside VLLM.

00:11:23.069 --> 00:11:28.009
Classic greedy bite pairing coding or BPE was proven to reach at least 0.36

00:11:28.009 --> 00:11:33.529
one of the optimal string length reduction for any string, budget and tie-breaking policy.

00:11:34.149 --> 00:11:40.229
Grox rate limits and fine print constraints, CIO reports affect practical usage more than headline pricing.

00:11:40.229 --> 00:11:46.649
OnDray Carpathi in a post on X called an unspecified artifact beautiful, said it was worth

00:11:46.649 --> 00:11:48.829
replicating and suggested building a few.

00:11:49.369 --> 00:11:55.989
Obtain a free ExoOn API key and test KExoOn 2.5 on Korean language agent or tool-calling

00:11:55.989 --> 00:11:58.109
tasks against your current open models.

00:11:58.749 --> 00:12:05.049
Wrap lengthy AI-generated pull request descriptions in HTML details and summary tags so GitHub pages

00:12:05.049 --> 00:12:05.729
stay readable.

00:12:05.729 --> 00:12:10.409
run the RL attack code on your own models to measure how quickly black box

00:12:10.409 --> 00:12:14.929
attacks can degrade performance on your specific tasks. Experiment with the

00:12:14.929 --> 00:12:18.469
background decision evaluation survey history schema on your own

00:12:18.469 --> 00:12:22.869
respondent data to see whether adding an evaluation block improves prediction

00:12:22.869 --> 00:12:27.775
accuracy. Teams addressing English-centric evaluation gaps are likely to

00:12:27.775 --> 00:12:32.775
publish more multilingual and low resource benchmarks. Black box attack methods

00:12:32.775 --> 00:12:37.275
and corresponding defenses will continue as the community studies model robustness.

00:12:37.595 --> 00:12:42.835
Before we go, free APIs and weights from more open-weight labs are expected in the coming weeks.

